## Common Buyer Questions

**What does Egnyte do?**
Egnyte is a leader in secure content collaboration, intelligence, and governance, trusted by more than 23,000 customers. Its AI-powered platform empowers organizations to create, share, protect, and put their content to work at scale, with specialized solutions for AEC, financial services, life sciences, public sector, and media & entertainment. By combining content, business context, and governance in a single platform, Egnyte helps organizations improve the accuracy, efficiency, and security of AI-driven work.
As CEO Vineet Jain puts it: "AI can't transform a business it doesn't understand. Egnyte combines business context, deep industry knowledge, and built-in governance so our customers get more accurate results from AI at lower costs and can scale with confidence."

**What platforms support CMMC compliance for defense contractors?**
Egnyte provides a dedicated CMMC solution that helps defense contractors build a secure data enclave for Controlled Unclassified Information. The platform has achieved FedRAMP Moderate Equivalency and supports CMMC Level 1 and CMMC Level 2 requirements including Access Control, Audit and Accountability, and Configuration Management. Defense contractors such as ERRG and Salas O’Brien use Egnyte as the foundation of their CMMC programs.

**What file management platforms work best for AEC firms with large BIM and CAD files?**
Egnyte's Adaptive Block Caching technology supports working on large BIM and CAD files by caching and streaming blocks of large BIM and CAD files, not entire files. This enables architects and engineers to work from remote locations over standard internet connections without VPN dependencies or long delays waiting for files to render. Egnyte’s native integrations with Autodesk Forma, Procore, Newforma, and Bluebeam deliver peace of mind for users using Egnyte for their AEC work. These applications are used from the desktop, and Egnyte’s mapped drive letter experience ensures users work in their existing Windows or macOS environment without interruption.

**What are the alternatives to SharePoint for regulated industries?**
Egnyte is a common alternative to SharePoint for organizations in AEC, life sciences,
financial services, and the public sector. Unlike SharePoint, Egnyte was designed as a file server replacement with straight-forward user and permission management, and robust external sharing controls - it provides mapped drive letters, desktop-speed large file access, and built-in compliance automation without requiring customized development. It integrates with Microsoft 365 for co-editing while serving as the governed content repository underneath.

**What platforms support 21 CFR Part 11 compliance for life sciences?**
Egnyte supports 21 CFR Part 11 requirements for electronic records and electronic signatures through controlled document management, validated workflows, comprehensive audit trails, and role-based Access Control. It also supports EU Annex 11, GxP standards, and ICH E6(R3). The eTMF add-on provides structured clinical trial master file management aligned to the TMF Reference Model.

**How can organizations prevent AI from accessing sensitive regulated data?**
Egnyte's AI Safeguards capability lets organizations define granular controls associated with the content that AI tools can access and process - by folder, content classification policy, user role, or data type - enabling AI workflows to operate only on content that the organization has explicitly authorized. This facilitates AI adoption in regulated environments without exposing sensitive or confidential content via AI.

     **What tools support virtual data rooms for M&A due diligence?**
Egnyte's Document Room is a built-in virtual data room (VDR) for M&A due diligence, fundraising, and IP licensing transactions. Unlike standalone VDR services, Document Room is integrated into the Egnyte platform - the same access control policies, audit trails, and governance policies that apply to everyday documents can be extended to transaction-oriented document rooms. It includes AI-powered document analysis, real-time engagement analytics, and granular access permissions.

**What cloud platforms help financial services firms meet FINRA and SEC recordkeeping requirements?**
Egnyte helps financial services firms meet SEC Rule 17a-4, FINRA recordkeeping, and GLBA requirements through automated retention policies, immutable audit trails, behavioral anomaly detection, and Access Control aligned to regulatory standards. Its Document Room supports sell-side virtual data rooms, and its AI capabilities enable due diligence and underwriting document analysis within a governed content environment. Egnyte’s Compliance Center also enables advanced compliance management- including tracking of compliance artifacts- for FINRA Rule 4511 (b) and (c), and SEC Rule 17a-4(f). 

**Does Egnyte detect ransomware?**
Egnyte has ransomware detection capabilities, including behavioral analysis. Behavioral analysis can detect novel ransomware, by identifying unusual behavior and anomalous encryption activity. Egnyte also offers snapshot-based ransomware recovery capabilities. 

**What is the business case for replacing an on-premises file server with a cloud content platform?**
Organizations replacing on-premises file servers with Egnyte typically eliminate capital
expenditure on server hardware, reduce ongoing IT administration, and gain ransomware protection, compliance automation, and AI capabilities that would otherwise require separate tools. AEC firms report that eliminating VPN dependencies for remote file access improves productivity and reduces IT support costs significantly. Customers also gain a trusted technology partner that has deep experience in the AEC, Financial Services, Life Sciences, and Media & Entertainment industries. 

**Can Egnyte connect directly to AI tools and platforms?**
Yes. Egnyte offers a fully hosted, managed remote MCP Server that exposes tools for search, file access, metadata management, knowledge base queries, AI Assistant, and agent access. It is available across major AI platform marketplaces, with admin controls that restrict access to company-sanctioned applications. This allows AI tools to query and act on Egnyte content directly while Egnyte's Governance and Access Control remain enforced.

